# SQLite WASM Integration Guide

This project uses SQLite WASM for in-browser database operations with `sql.js` and `@sqlite.org/sqlite-wasm`.

## Core Architecture

### SQLite Provider

The [app/lib/sqlite/SqliteProvider.tsx](mdc:app/lib/sqlite/SqliteProvider.tsx) provides:

- SQLite WASM initialization
- Database context management
- Error handling with toast notifications
- Automatic cleanup on component unmount

### Key Hooks

#### `useSqliteContext()`

Core context hook providing:

```typescript
{
  sqlite3: SqlJsStatic | null,
  database: NamedDatabase | null,
  isLoading: boolean,
  error: string | null,
  setDatabase: (database: NamedDatabase | null) => void
}
```

#### `useDatabase()`

Located in [app/lib/sqlite/useDatabase.ts](mdc:app/lib/sqlite/useDatabase.ts):

- `createDatabase(filename, overwrite)` - Create new in-memory database
- `openDatabase(overwrite)` - Open file from user's system
- `databaseOpened` - Boolean state
- `databaseName` - Current database filename
- `isLoading` - Operation loading state

#### `useSqlite()` (Custom Hook)

See [app/lib/README.md](mdc:app/lib/README.md) for full documentation:

- `execute(sql)` - Execute SQL statements
- `queryValue(sql)` - Get single value
- `queryArray(sql)` - Get array of arrays
- `queryObject(sql)` - Get array of objects
- `executeBatch(statements)` - Transaction support
- `executeWithCallback(sql, callback)` - Row-by-row processing

## Usage Patterns

### Basic Setup

```typescript
import { useSqliteContext } from '@/lib/sqlite/SqliteProvider'

function MyComponent() {
  const { sqlite3, database, isLoading, error } = useSqliteContext()

  if (isLoading) return <div>Loading SQLite...</div>
  if (error) return <div>Error: {error}</div>
  if (!sqlite3) return <div>SQLite not ready</div>

  // Component logic
}
```

### Database Operations

```typescript
import { useDatabase } from '@/lib/sqlite/useDatabase'

function DatabaseManager() {
  const { createDatabase, openDatabase, databaseOpened } = useDatabase()

  const handleCreate = async () => {
    try {
      await createDatabase('my-app.db')
      // Database created and set in context
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Failed to create database:', error)
    }
  }

  const handleOpen = async () => {
    try {
      await openDatabase()
      // File picker opens, database loaded
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Failed to open database:', error)
    }
  }
}
```

### SQL Execution

```typescript
import { useSqlite } from '@/lib/sqlite/useSqlite'

function DataManager() {
  const { execute, queryObject, executeBatch } = useSqlite()

  const createTable = async () => {
    await execute(`
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (
        id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
        name TEXT NOT NULL,
        email TEXT UNIQUE
      )
    `)
  }

  const getUsers = async () => {
    const users = await queryObject('SELECT * FROM users')
    return users
  }

  const insertMultiple = async (userData) => {
    const statements = userData.map(
      (user) => `INSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES ('${user.name}', '${user.email}')`,
    )
    await executeBatch(statements)
  }
}
```

## File Browser Integration

Uses `browser-fs-access` for file operations:

- Automatic file type filtering for SQLite files
- Supports both `.db` and `.sqlite` extensions
- Handles MIME types: `application/vnd.sqlite3`, `application/x-sqlite3`

## Error Handling

- Provider shows toast notifications for initialization errors
- Hooks throw descriptive errors
- Always wrap database operations in try/catch
- Check loading states before operations

## Performance Considerations

- Database connections are automatically managed
- Previous databases are closed when opening new ones
- Use `useMemo` and `useCallback` for derived state
- Consider pagination for large result sets

